WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.890
Our classroom fan was on all

2
00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:04.990
night, with nobody in the room!

3
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.060
A fan needs to decide.

4
00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.350
Is it hot, and is someone here?

5
00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:12.770
Today: decisions.

6
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.340
If this, then that.

7
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:18.690
A decision starts with if.

8
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.800
If it is raining, then take an umbrella.

9
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.560
The if part is a question: is it raining?

10
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.970
The answer is yes or no.

11
00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.460
Else tells the robot what to do

12
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.680
when the answer is no.

13
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:35.410
If the light is red, stop.

14
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.900
Else, if it isn’t red, go.

15
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.960
Every if is a fork in the road.

16
00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:45.150
Some decisions ask two questions.

17
00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.560
The fan goes on if it is hot AND

18
00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:49.840
someone is in the room.

19
00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.700
Both must be yes.

20
00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.180
With OR, one yes is enough.

21
00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:57.950
Decisions are everywhere.

22
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.900
A street light: if it is dark, switch on.

23
00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.990
A game: if a player who isn’t the

24
00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:06.950
goalkeeper touches the ball with their

25
00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.330
hand on purpose, it’s a free kick.

26
00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:11.980
Your phone: if the battery is

27
00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.460
low, show a warning.

28
00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:15.200
Quick check!

29
00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:19.340
The rule is: fan on if it is

30
00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:22.120
hot AND someone is in.

31
00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.100
It is hot, but the room is empty.

32
00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.360
Does the fan go on?

33
00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:28.800
No.

34
00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.210
AND needs both answers to be yes,

35
00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.770
and nobody is in the room.

36
00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.510
That saves electricity all night!

37
00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:41.170
In the app, open Logic gates.

38
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.210
Flip the switches and watch the lamp.

39
00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.550
Then solve the Fan puzzle: test every

40
00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.470
row until all of them are right.

41
00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:51.200
Your turn.

42
00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.850
The alarm rings if the door

43
00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.470
OR the window opens.

44
00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:57.750
Only the window opens.

45
00:01:58.630 --> 00:01:59.390
Does it ring?

46
00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:01.630
Yes, it rings.

47
00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.160
Remember: if asks a yes or no question.

48
00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:07.880
Else says what to do when

49
00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:08.980
the answer is no.

50
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.780
AND needs both; OR needs one.

51
00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.390
Try it yourself: play If this,

52
00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:17.950
then that with your family.

53
00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:21.640
One person says a rule, like: if you

54
00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.320
are wearing blue, stand up.

55
00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.080
Everyone checks the rule, and

56
00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.860
does it only if it’s true.
